@startuml
title Car Park Provider API - TfNSW Upstream Contract
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

package "Upstream Car Park API" {
  interface CarParkApi
  class FacilityCatalog <<provider payload>> {
    facility IDs
    facility names
  }
  class CarParkApiRecord <<provider payload>> {
    facilityId : provider identifier
    facilityName
    spots
    occupancy
    messageDate : Sydney local wall time (no offset)
  }
  class HistoryQuery {
    facility
    eventdate : YYYY-MM-DD
  }
  CarParkApi --> FacilityCatalog : GET /carpark without facility
  CarParkApi --> CarParkApiRecord : GET /carpark?facility={id}
  CarParkApi --> HistoryQuery : accepts eventdate/facility
  CarParkApi --> "0..*" CarParkApiRecord : GET /carpark/history
}

note left of CarParkApiRecord
  The service's provider adapter interprets MessageDate as
  Australia/Sydney local time, then converts it to an Instant.
  Do not parse it as UTC: the value has no offset. The normalized
  domain stores the resulting instant in UTC. An offset-free Sydney
  wall time can be ambiguous during clock changes; apply the documented
  overlap policy at the provider boundary.
end note

note right of CarParkApi
  carparkswagger_prod_2.yaml documents /carpark,
  /carpark?facility=..., and /carpark/history. Its success
  schemas are opaque `file` types, so the Java provider DTO
  and observed payloads currently supply field-level details.
end note

@enduml
